  "implementation": "Canonical C socket and result layouts include atomic reference credits. udp.native.c includes the existing udp.sn.c implementation through standalone aliases. Socket registry and WinSock initialization are serialized for independent sockets. Final release closes only registered sockets; default zero descriptor records cannot close stdin. Result getter arrays and strings own independent copies.",
  "independent_controls": "C and Rust archive clients verify sizeof/offsets, nil/default/empty states, binary datagrams, owner aliases and credits, returned bytes/senders surviving result release, repeated dispose, final-release descriptor closure on POSIX, and eight threads each creating32 independent sockets.",
